# CHANGELOG

## 20260807

0.3.0: Rewrite CHANGELOG.txt as a CHANGELOG in the form changelogger writes, and add the entries for 0.0.0 and 0.1.0.

1. /CHANGELOG.txt/CHANGELOG/, rewritten with a dated heading per version, the version and its summary on the first line of the body, then the numbered items. The old form carried neither a date nor a summary line, so a commit message could not be taken from it, which is half of what a CHANGELOG is for here.
2. + Entries for 0.0.0 and 0.1.0, which the file had never reached back to. Both come from changelogger, run over the revisions staged out of the git history, tier 3 inventorying the first and tier 2 diffing the second. Their summaries are written here, tier 2 recording none and tier 3 offering only "(Initial version)", neither of which would serve as a commit message. 0.1.0's rename is added by hand too, tier 2 as it then was comparing structure and so seeing nothing of a change made in a comment.
3. The entries for 0.2.0 and 0.2.1 are carried across as written, being better than anything a structural diff would produce.


## 20260807

0.2.1: Make the script executable.

1. ~ bin/git-checkout-new-issue: mode 100644 --> 100755. A script carrying a shebang and not the bit to go with it cannot be run from a clone at all. Homebrew's bin.install had been setting the bit on the way past, so nothing showed until the formula moved to libexec.install, which keeps whatever mode the repository has.


## 20240318

0.2.0: Add a README, so that Homebrew installs the repository correctly.

1. + README.md: Having a second file in the root of the repo means that Homebrew will install this correctly. No shit.
2. + CHANGELOG.txt: While I was at it.
3. ~ bin/git-checkout-new-issue: Move the notes to README.md.


